[
    {
        "content": "<p>Propsal: <code>deriving Repr</code> should add <code>[Repr X]</code> binders for each nested type <code>X</code> discovered, rather than synthesizing <code>Repr X</code> during the derivation.</p>\n<p>Consider this example</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: { x1 := 100, x2 := 200 } -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">200</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">reducible</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instance</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hexRepr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">reprPrec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"0x\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toDigits</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- doesn't change</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: { x1 := 100, x2 := 200 } -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">200</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>here the generated declaration is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">instReprMyFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which hard-codes the needed repr instances at derivation time. The derived instance could instead accept <code>[Repr UInt64]</code> binders, such that the behavior was as follows:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- `deriving Repr` should produce this instead, with `[Repr UInt64]`</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instReprMyFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">reprPrec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instReprMyFoo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr'</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">repr'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">prec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bracket</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"{ \"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nil</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"x1\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f!</span><span class=\"s2\">\" := \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nest</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f!</span><span class=\"s2\">\",\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"x2\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f!</span><span class=\"s2\">\" := \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nest</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">group</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" }\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: { x1 := 100, x2 := 200 } -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">200</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">reducible</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instance</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hexRepr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">reprPrec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"0x\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toDigits</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: { x1 := 0x64, x2 := 0xc8 } -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyFoo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">200</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 593132641,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778027098
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The motivation here would be to allow customing Repr instances for debugging purposes, without having to rederive all downstream repr instances.</p>",
        "id": 593132721,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778027160
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Seems reasonable! I wonder if we could even lint for this in hand-written <code>Repr</code>s.</p>",
        "id": 593133116,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1778027372
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess the question also arises for <code>ToMessageData</code>, and maybe even <code>ToExpr</code>. I guess the claim that \"there should only be one instance of this typeclass\" applies less to debugging tools than to things like <code>Add</code>?</p>",
        "id": 593136189,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778029503
    }
]